OL,3,GNEWSAPlans for year-round dog ban on
OL,4,Abeach to be scaled back
OL,5,
OL,6,FPlans for a year-round dog ban on part
OL,7,Fof a north Wales beach are set to be
OL,8,Fscaled back following demonstrations
OL,9,Fand public anger.
OL,11,FIn August, hundreds of dog owners took
OL,12,Ftheir pets to Rhos-on-Sea beach to
OL,13,Fprotest against the proposed ban on the
OL,14,FCayley Promenade section, which is
OL,15,Falready between dog-free areas.
OL,17,FConwy councillors have voted for the
OL,18,FDog Control Public Spaces Protection
OL,19,FOrder, originally proposed as
OL,20,Fyear-round, to be in place from 1 May
OL,21,Fto 30 September, although final
OL,22,Fapproval must be made by the cabinet.
OL,23,APub: 16-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,439,430,260,140,0,100
